# 6. LinkedIn Integration

## 6.1 LinkedIn OAuth

Users connect LinkedIn through OAuth and never provide their LinkedIn password to the application.

Flow:

```text
Dashboard
    ↓
Connect LinkedIn
    ↓
LinkedIn OAuth
    ↓
Permission Request
    ↓
Authorization
    ↓
Backend Token Handling
    ↓
Connected
```

UI states:

- Not connected
- Connecting
- Connected
- Error
- Disconnect

Requested permissions must be explained clearly.

## 6.2 Token Security

LinkedIn tokens must:

- Remain server-side
- Never be unnecessarily returned to the frontend
- Never appear in logs
- Never be committed to Git
- Be securely stored/encrypted where appropriate
- Be associated with the correct application user

Client secrets remain server-side.

## 6.3 Supported API Only

Use currently supported LinkedIn API capabilities.

Do not implement:

- Password-based LinkedIn login
- CAPTCHA bypass
- Rate-limit bypass
- Anti-bot bypass
- Browser automation intended to bypass controls
- Credential scraping
- Unauthorized scraping

The application must not assume that every LinkedIn capability is available. Required products/permissions must be verified before implementation.

